load ../stats-fold.maude

--- Coverage: two runs of the SAME grain under one key fold to ONE row. This is
--- the search that makes the bite below non-vacuous — merging is a rule that
--- really fires, so the third search failing is a property and not an absence.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STATS-FOLD :
  run(r1, gcall) run(r1, gcall)
  =>! rowFor(r1, gcall) .

--- Coverage: two runs of DIFFERENT grain under one key fold to TWO rows,
--- because grain is part of the group key (DR-0114 clause 2).
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STATS-FOLD :
  run(r1, gcall) run(r1, gturn)
  =>! rowFor(r1, gcall) rowFor(r1, gturn) .

--- Bite: grouping by rule alone can NEVER collapse two grains into one row.
--- Relax the merge rule to match two different grains and this finds a solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STATS-FOLD :
  run(r1, gcall) run(r1, gturn)
  =>! rowFor(r1, gcall) .

--- Coverage: recorded contributions fold to a recorded measure.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STATS-FOLD :
  folded(val) contrib(val) contrib(val)
  =>! folded(val) .

--- Coverage: one unrecorded contribution makes the folded measure unrecorded,
--- however many recorded ones accompany it (DR-0114 clause 1).
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STATS-FOLD :
  folded(val) contrib(val) contrib(nul)
  =>! folded(nul) .

--- Bite: an unrecorded contribution can never leave the folded measure
--- recorded. This is the per-measure clause, which population tagging alone
--- does not reach: both contributions here sit in ONE row at one grain.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STATS-FOLD :
  folded(val) contrib(val) contrib(nul)
  =>! folded(val) .

--- Coverage: a run carrying per-call rows is counted once, through the
--- per-call path, which consumes its turn sum with it.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STATS-FOLD :
  callRows turnSum
  =>* counted RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: a run carrying only a turn sum is counted through the sum path.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STATS-FOLD :
  turnSum
  =>! counted .

--- Bite: a run is never counted twice. The RESIDUAL soup variable means a
--- second `counted` in ANY reachable state is a solution, so No solution proves
--- the two folding paths cannot both claim one run. Add a rule folding
--- `callRows` on its own and this finds a solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-STATS-FOLD :
  callRows turnSum
  =>* counted counted RESIDUAL:Cfg .
